description:
Plan against docs/plans/2026-10-30-per-task-worktrees.md §7.3 and §7.4.

Objective: an operator can tell offline whether a project is ready for worktree mode, and has a written stop-the-world runbook to turn it on and to roll it back. A human performs the flip; no Moe seat ever merges moe/work-* into main.

Deliverable:
- commands/doctor.ts gains worktree probes. They are reported as info when resolveWorktreeMode(settings) (WT-01, task-6cf120a38b344e72b7bab8b9faf806f1) is 'off', and as hard checks when it is 'on':
  - git >= 2.38;
  - the project is its repository's top level;
  - the control checkout's HEAD is refs/heads/moe/control;
  - the target (literal consolidationBranch, else main) exists and is not checked out in any worktree;
  - a soft warning for registered .worktrees/* whose task is DONE or ARCHIVED for more than 24 h (the sweep falling behind).
- Tests in commands/doctor.test.ts.
- docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md gains a 'Worktree mode: flip on / roll back' section with the §7.3 and §7.4 runbooks verbatim in substance: drain, the rescue-ref check, the human merge of moe/work-2026-10-24 into main, `git switch -c moe/control main`, the settings (worktreeMode, consolidationBranch main, the git-land-main resource with releaseOnDeregister true), doctor, restart; and rollback.

NOT in scope: changing the default (WT-19); wrapper changes; other docs (WT-17/WT-18).

Verification: cd packages/moe-daemon && npm run build && npx vitest run src/commands/doctor.test.ts
